/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - A packed absorber is a vertical shell filled with small shaped pieces or a corrugated sheet stack.
   - Three numbers describe a packing.
   - Ap is the total surface area of the packing in m²; Vbed is the packed-bed volume in m³; Vvoid is the void volume in m³.
   - Plot pressure drop per metre of bed ΔP/Z against gas mass flux G.
   - More liquid fills more of the voids, so a higher liquid rate floods at a lower gas rate.
   - Gdesign is the design gas mass flux in kg/(m²·s); Gflood is the flooding gas mass flux at the same liquid rate, from the pressure-drop curve or the correlation in Chapter 3.7.
   - A liquid distributor at the top spreads liquid evenly over the whole cross-section.
   - HETP, height equivalent to a theoretical plate, is the bed height that does one equilibrium stage; it is measured for a packing and used to size towers.
*/
